---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Masthead from '../../components/Masthead.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/Fact.astro';
import TargetPanels from '../../components/TargetPanels.astro';
import CallingConvention from '../../components/CallingConvention.astro';
import GfaBinding from '../../components/GfaBinding.astro';
import BitLayout from '../../components/BitLayout.astro';
import SourceList from '../../components/SourceList.astro';
import { manualBreadcrumbs } from '../../data/manual-structure';
import abi from '../../data/abi.json';
---
<Layout title="CUIS ABI" description="Private pTOS x32 CUIS selector and session query" running="AES"
  breadcrumbs={manualBreadcrumbs('aes')}>
  <article>
    <Masthead name="CUIS ABI" title="Controlled user interface services" subsystem="Private kernel ABI" />
    <dl class="prm-facts">
      <Fact label="Operation">Query whether the calling process owns a live CUIS session.</Fact>
      <Fact label="Selector"><code>CUIS_SERVICE_CLASS</code> <code>0x103</code> · <code>CUIS_SESSION_QUERY</code> <code>1</code></Fact>
      <Fact label="Availability">pTOS · x32 ring 3 with <code>CONF_WITH_CUIS</code>.
        The private ABI backs experimental userspace libaes on x32. Public GEM programs use <a href="/reference/appl_init/">GEMlib and libaes</a>.</Fact>
    </dl>
    <TargetPanels>
      <CallingConvention slot="68k" binding={{ status: 'unsupported', scope: '68k at this pTOS revision',
        detail: 'The CUIS class is compiled only for x86-64 user address spaces. There is no 68k CUIS trap.' }} />
      <CallingConvention slot="arm" binding={{ status: 'unsupported', scope: 'ARM at this pTOS revision',
        detail: 'The CUIS class is compiled only for x86-64 user address spaces. There is no ARM CUIS SVC.' }} />
      <CallingConvention slot="x32" binding={{ status: 'experimental', scope: 'x32 · CONF_WITH_CUIS',
        detail: 'Enter the kernel with SYSCALL from ring 3. RCX and R11 are clobbered. With CUIS disabled the dispatcher returns EINVFN.',
        registers: [['RAX', '64-bit selector on entry, sign-extended status on return'], ['RDI', 'Session handle, a scalar in the range 0 through 0x7FFFFFFF']] }}>
        <h3 class="prm-section-heading">Instruction / Data Format</h3>
        <BitLayout {...abi.cuis.selector} />
        <pre class="prm-code"><code>RAX = (trap_class &lt;&lt; 32) | function_number<br />RAX = {abi.cuis.example}</code></pre>
        <p><code>E_OK</code> (0) indicates a live endpoint owned by the calling PROCESS. <code>EACCDN</code> indicates no matching owned endpoint. <code>EINVAL</code> indicates an out-of-range handle.</p>
        <h3 class="prm-section-heading">Private Transport Calls in PR #903</h3>
        <p>These selectors are used inside pTOS and libaes. Arguments occupy <code>RDI, RSI, RDX, R10, R8, R9</code> in order.
          Each call selects the same class in RAX with its own function number. Application programs use documented GEM functions.</p>
        <table class="prm-rule-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Function</th><th scope="col">Selector</th><th scope="col">Arguments in register order</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>CUIS_LAUNCH_ATTACH</code></th><td>93</td><td><code>session, authorization, path, tail, environment, directory</code></td><td>Attach an optional console lease or observation receipt to a native PROCESS launch, then commit it.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>CUIS_STREAM_RECEIPT</code></th><td>94</td><td><code>session, action, address, size</code></td><td>Manage publication receipts using the 64-byte, 4-aligned record in <code>cuis_receipt.h</code>. QUERY is non-consuming.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>CUIS_ENDPOINT_BARRIER</code></th><td>95</td><td><code>session, action, token</code></td><td>Freeze endpoint registration with ACQUIRE (0), then release the matching owner and generation with RELEASE (1).</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>CUIS_STREAM_BATCH</code></th><td>96</td><td><code>session, command, a, b, c, d</code></td><td>Stage, seal, query, read, publish or settle bounded request and reply packets. The high command word selects the operation.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>SESSION_START (0) accepts <code>CUIS_SESSION_NEW</code> to allocate an additional endpoint owned by the same PROCESS.
          PEER_QUERY (76) can return the fixed-width client/PROCESS identity or resolve a client ID to a handle with
          <code>CUIS_PEER_IDENTITY</code> and <code>CUIS_PEER_HANDLE</code>. SESSION_WAIT (32) can wait on an array of up to 16 owned PROCESS rights.</p>
        <p>PROCESS launch and observation are handled by <a href="/reference/s-procexec/">S_PROCEXEC</a>. PR #903 removes the older CHILD and COHORT selectors. An endpoint handle and a GUI client ID are distinct from the owning PROCESS number and MiNT PID.</p>
      </CallingConvention>
      <GfaBinding slot="gfa" />
    </TargetPanels>
    <section aria-labelledby="related-heading">
      <h2 id="related-heading" class="prm-section-heading ruled">See Also</h2>
      <ul class="related-links"><li><a href="/reference/appl_init/">appl_init</a></li><li><a href="/abi/elf-entry/">ELF32 process entry</a></li></ul>
    </section>
    <SourceList sources={[
      ['ptos', 'include/cuis.h', 'Service class and opcode constants'],
      ['ptos', 'aes/Kconfig', 'CUIS build constraints'],
      ['ptos', 'bios/arch/x86_64/trap.c', 'x32 dispatch and privilege checks'],
      ['ptos', 'aes/cuis_session.c', 'Session ownership and return codes'],
      ['ptos', 'include/cuis_receipt.h', 'Receipt record and operation fields'],
      ['ptos', 'doc/cuis.txt', 'Private launch, receipt, barrier and stream batch contracts'],
      ['ptos', 'tests/cuis/program.c', 'Native syscall and invalid-handle probes'],
    ]} />
  </article>
</Layout>
